{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And they spoke</b> — to arrange a table, a metaphor for the meat." "<b>in the wilderness</b> — a place where there is no settlement."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads לערוך שלחן (\"to arrange a table\"); Ibn Ezra may be glossing an inferred meaning of the phrase לערוך שלחן in the verse as referring to the request for meat, but the comment is terse and offered as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:00.758144840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}